  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5605.17 Commissioner's Discretion",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5605.17 Commissioner's Discretion.\n\n(a) The commissioner may refuse to release records which are requested pursuant to RSA 260:14 in any particular case if he determines that such a release may be contrary to the public interest or would constitute an unwarranted invasion of privacy.\n\n(b) The commissioner may accept faxed requests for information, and all faxed opt-outs shall be honored.\n\n(c) The commissioner is authorized to obtain such further information as he shall deem necessary prior to releasing any motor vehicle drivers' records.\n\n(d) The commissioner shall have the authority to determine what mode of access a requestor may use to obtain motor vehicle records.\n\n(e) The commissioner shall have the authority to charge any requestor, including government requests, for motor vehicle records.\n\nSource. #7361, EXEMPT, eff 9-1-00; ss by #7621, EXEMPT, eff 1-1-02",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5600.html"
